# Crag Hydra — a Strong enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 8/12 Strong enemies — 22 life, bribe 100 gold
# enemy: Hydra — the 1997 in-game name (s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES); the deck file, s30 and the wiki call it "Crag Hydra"
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0207.dck "Crag Hydra (R, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 12 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 13 lines (60
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/crag_hydra.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 8)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/crag_hydra.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Strong) — "Crag Hydra" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Crag Hydra
22 Mountain
4 Mana Flare
4 Power Surge
4 Fireball
2 Lightning Bolt
4 Inferno
4 Onulet
4 Wall of Fire
4 Disintegrate
1 Detonate
2 Soul Net
2 Shivan Dragon
3 The Hive
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 The Hive
#   .vBlack  3 The Hive
#   .vBlue   1 Red Elemental Blast, 2 The Hive
#   .vGreen  3 The Hive
#   .vRed    3 The Hive
#   .vWhite  3 The Hive
SB: 1 Red Elemental Blast
